  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 129 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nBeginning Friday, we see the weather pattern shift as the upper-\nlevel high establishes itself in the southeast US. The anticyclonic \nrotation will circulate dry air into the southeastern half of the \ncombined Panhandles, stifling PoP chances. However, upper-level \nsupport from shortwave perturbations on the western periphery of the \nupper-level high (PVA and upper level divergence) will establish a \npattern of increased PoP chances in the western/northwestern \nPanhandles through the weekend. There is still the question of \nintensity and spatial coverage, as long-range models do not have the \nspatial resolution to clarify this yet. However, a persistent signal \nof PoP chances have been in this area throughout the week, which is \nincreasing confidence as we get closer to the event window. \n\nPast the weekend PoP chances, hot and dry conditions are expected to \nreturn due to the retrograding of the upper-kllevel high back to the \nwest and over the Panhandles. The end of the forecast period shows \nupper-level flow flattening out over the central US, which could in \nturn pull the jet closer to the southern plains, but this signal is \ntoo far out for much confidence. \n\nFerguson",
